- verify whether first-party Cacophony messaging tools are registered/injected and permit the canary to send/read project-scoped messages under its exact agent credential;
- provide the reviewed shell/command surface expected by the declared canary profile, with cwd/checkout isolation, timeout/output bounds, and explicit capability authorization; do not grant ambient unrestricted host shell merely to satisfy the test;
- ensure remote web/TUI continuation preserves the same tool catalog and credentials as the host-local session;
- add an end-to-end canary fixture asserting filesystem read, project-scoped Cacophony message access, and one harmless bounded shell command when that capability is declared;
- fail with a precise configuration/capability omission receipt rather than silently presenting a reduced filesystem-only catalog.

Observed 2026-08-08 on ms-dev-4 and remote ms-dev-3 by Harry. No work was claimed and no source/provider/config/service mutation occurred during the observation.


