# bd-833b3e — put pinned Bash on Nix package-check PATH

## Correction to landed bd-9e82f5 / e736204

The landed test changed `/bin/bash` to `process.env.BASH || "bash"`. Local 6/6
passed because helsinki's interactive environment has
`BASH=/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash`.

Hosted Nix check proves that environment assumption is false inside the package
derivation: BASH is unset and `bash` is not on PATH. Exact runs `30810507444` and
`30811475306`, plus main CI run `30825859803`, fail all four retry behavior tests
with ENOENT/exit 126 before hydration.

This is the coordinating agent's second test-environment design error; the fresh
worker implemented the requested patch correctly.

## Fix

Add pinned Bash to package `nativeBuildInputs`:

```nix
nativeBuildInputs = [ pkgs.makeWrapper pkgs.openssl pkgs.bash ];
```

Keep JavaScript's `process.env.BASH || "bash"`; in Nix, `pkgs.bash` provides the
PATH executable, while ordinary hosts use their environment. Extend regression
to assert the flake supplies pinned Bash as well as rejecting `/bin/bash`.

## Validation in disposable current-main clone

- full `test/npm-deps-retry.test.mjs`: 6/6 PASS on helsinki NixOS
- Nix package derivation eval: PASS
  `/nix/store/n8hr7j44pfcab24zs5aglqx8z2ww17wd-pi-daemon-0.3.0.drv`
- two-file exact scope; no canonical checkout/host mutation

Hosted delivery remains authoritative for the Nix sandbox instance.

